class ConceptSystemMember {
  definition {
    Abstract base shape for a member of any n-ary concept-system
    relation — PartitiveRelation, GenericRelation, and future
    AssociativeRelation / SequentialRelation.

    Carries the ISO 704:2022 MECE dimensions on every member:
      presence      — required (default) | optional
      count         — exactly_one (default) | at_least_one | multiple
      is_delimiting — false (default) | true

    These three dimensions are orthogonal and apply uniformly across
    all n-ary relation types. The combination (optional, at_least_one)
    is invalid and collapses to (optional, multiple).

    LUTAML files do not express inheritance — each leaf class
    (PartitiveMember, GenericMember) re-declares these fields with
    leaf-specific documentation. Ruby/JS consumers use real inheritance
    from a ConceptSystemMember base class. See
    docs/design/abstract-nary-relation.md.

    The abstract shape is the canonical reference; the leaves exist for
    type safety in code and to leave room for type-specific extensions
    (e.g., AssociativeMember will gain a `role` field).
  }
  +ref: <<StandardDocument>> ReferenceToTermbase [1] {
    definition {
      The target concept of this relation member. Encoded as a
      ConceptRef (source + id, optional text), same shape as
      RelatedConcept#ref.

      For Partitive: the partitive concept (subordinate).
      For Generic: the specific concept (species).
    }
  }
  +presence: PartitivePresence [0..1] {
    definition {
      Whether this member must exist in every instance (required) or
      may exist only in some instances (optional).

      ISO 704:2022 encodes this as the line style: solid (required) vs
      dashed (optional). Defaults to required when omitted.

      Field name retains "partitive" prefix for backward compatibility
      with existing SKOS taxonomy URIs; the dimension itself applies
      to all n-ary relation types uniformly.
    }
  }
  +count: PartitiveCount [0..1] {
    definition {
      How many instances of this member exist. ISO 704:2022 encodes
      this via the number of lines in the diagram notation.

      Defaults to exactly_one when omitted. The combination
      presence: optional + count: at_least_one is invalid.
    }
  }
  +is_delimiting: Boolean [0..1] {
    definition {
      ISO 704:2022 delimiting part (bold 3x-width line in diagram).
      When true, this member behaves like a delimiting characteristic:
      it distinguishes the comprehensive from coordinate concepts.

      Orthogonal to presence and count. Defaults to false when omitted.

      Contextual to the relation it belongs to — the same part may be
      delimiting in one PartitiveRelation and not in another.
    }
  }
}
